</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Effectiveness of Weighted Average Voting.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct the ablation study on the Weighted Average Voting technique introduced in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Weighted Average Voting for Output Selection ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ MITS: Enhanced Tree Search Reasoning for LLMs via Pointwise Mutual Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, evaluating the impact of selecting different numbers of top-scoring reasoning paths <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> for final answer selection. Using model <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Qwen2.5-3B</span>, we run MITS with beam width of 32 across all three datasets and vary <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> from 1 to 32. The corresponding performance results are reported in Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Effectiveness of Weighted Average Voting. ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MITS: Enhanced Tree Search Reasoning for LLMs via Pointwise Mutual Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
The results show consistent performance improvements as <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases, with the steepest gains observed at small <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> values (<span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, ARC-Challenge improves from 84.31% to 89.12% as <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases from 1 to 8).
Optimal <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> values are dataset-dependent: StrategyQA peaks at <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=16</annotation></semantics></math> while ARC-Challenge and CommonsenseQA achieve best results at <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=32</annotation></semantics></math>. Performance stabilizes as <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> value becomes larger, indicating diminishing returns from incorporating additional reasoning paths.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Performance across different values of top-<math id="S4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> for weighted majority voting with <span id="S4.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Qwen2.5-3B</span>. Best results for each dataset are in <span id="S4.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</figcaption>
